  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Visit",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/validate.cc",
    "description": "In ValidateArrayDataVisitor::Visit(const UnionArray&), the code calls array.IsNull(i) while iterating i < array.length() without first validating that the union array\u2019s null bitmap is large enough for length+offset. IsNull() dereferences BitUtil::GetBit(null_bitmap_data_, i + offset) directly, so a malformed IPC union array with inconsistent bitmap buffer size causes an out-of-bounds read and SEGV in GetBit.",
    "conditions": "FuzzIpcStream in arrow/cpp/src/arrow/ipc/reader.cc reads attacker-controlled IPC stream data into RecordBatches, then calls batch->ValidateFull(). For this PoV, a crafted union array is accepted far enough that ValidateArrayDataVisitor::Visit(UnionArray) runs; the array has a non-null null_bitmap_data_ pointer but an invalid/too-short bitmap relative to array.length()/offset. During the null check loop (array.IsNull(i)), GetBit reads past the bitmap buffer and crashes."
  },
